win10xbox: the builtins' version resources do not say Wine

GetFileVersionInfoW on ntdll.dll / kernel32.dll / user32.dll returned ProductName "Wine 11.9", FileDescription
"Wine ntdll", LegalCopyright "... the Wine project authors ..." and, for ntdll and user32, the file versions
6.1.7601.24059 and 5.1.2600.2180 (kernel32 carried 10.0.19045.5796, the default of ntverp.h).
CompanyName already was "Microsoft Corporation" (the comment in ntverp.h.in: GameGuard depends on it).

* ProductName: the string Windows reports. LegalCopyright: the license the binaries are under, without a
  Microsoft or Wine copyright claim (the LGPL text and source ship next to the DLLs).
* FileDescription: ntdll "NT Layer DLL", kernel32 "Windows NT BASE API Client DLL", user32
  "Multi-User Windows USER API Client DLL" (what Windows 10 reports); every other module of dlls.txt loses
  its "Wine " prefix, and the generated default is the module name instead of "Wine <name>".
* The default product/file version of ntverp.h becomes 10.0.19045.3803: Windows 10 22H2 with the update
  revision machine/machine.default.json gives the guest (windows.ubr), instead of Wine's own 5796. ntdll and
  user32 lose their Windows 7 / XP numbers and take it.

